---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBanner from '../components/CtaBanner.astro';
import FeatureCard from '../components/FeatureCard.astro';

const title = 'About Us';
const description =
  'Trading Yantra is built by traders who wanted a stock analysis tool that reports measured evidence honestly — including when a popular pattern has no real edge.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/about">
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-line">
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-[420px] bg-radial-fade"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-20 text-center sm:px-6 sm:py-28 lg:px-8">
      <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-line bg-surface px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-teal-300">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-teal-400"></span>
        About Trading Yantra
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
        A "yantra" is an instrument. <span class="text-gradient-brand">So is this.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        In Sanskrit, a <em class="text-slate-300 not-italic font-semibold">yantra</em> is a precise
        geometric instrument built for a single purpose. Ours is built to turn raw NSE &amp; BSE
        market data into a signal a retail trader can actually reason about.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="prose-invert space-y-6 text-slate-300">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Why we built this</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Retail traders in India are not short on tools. They're short on tools that tell the truth
        about themselves. Most signal services show you the win streak and quietly bury the losing
        stretch. Most "AI-powered" trading apps treat the model as a black box and ask you to trust
        the output on faith.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Trading Yantra started from a simpler premise: build the kind of analysis tool we'd actually
        want to trade with ourselves — one where every rule, pattern and model signal is backed by a
        measurement we can point to, and where a negative result is reported as clearly as a positive
        one.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-white">How we approach the problem</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        We combine three layers instead of leaning on any single one:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-teal-400">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">A technical indicator engine</strong> — RSI, EMA, ADX, ATR,
          Bollinger Bands and Williams %R computed daily and screened into buy/sell signals.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">A candlestick &amp; price-action engine</strong> — twelve
          candlestick detectors plus a point-in-time context model (trend, pullback,
          support/resistance, volume, relative strength, volatility and market regime) that scores
          every pattern <em>in context</em>, benchmarked against an unconditional baseline.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">AI/ML models</strong> — trained on historical NSE/BSE price
          action to surface signals that classic rule-based indicators can miss.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        None of these three layers is presented as infallible. Each is a hypothesis that gets tested
        against real, measured outcomes — and the product reflects what the testing actually shows,
        not what would be easiest to market.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-white">What "radical honesty" means in practice</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Concretely: when our research shows that a popular chart-pattern breakout underperforms a
        random baseline, that finding ships in the product's own documentation instead of being
        quietly dropped. When a market regime looks unfavorable, the product can shrink or veto
        position sizing rather than firing a signal blind to the broader trend. We'd rather be useful
        than impressive.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-line bg-ink-soft">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">What we stand for</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <FeatureCard
          icon="shield"
          title="Evidence over hype"
          description="Every signal traces back to a measured result. If something doesn't work, we say so — in the product, not just the fine print."
        />
        <FeatureCard
          icon="chart-pattern"
          title="Context over rules"
          description="A pattern in isolation means little. We score trend, volume, support/resistance and regime together before calling a signal."
        />
        <FeatureCard
          icon="bell"
          title="Risk-aware by design"
          description="Position sizing responds to market regime instead of treating every signal as equally safe to act on."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 text-center sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Before you rely on anything here</h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
      Trading Yantra is a technology and analytics product, not a SEBI-registered investment adviser,
      and nothing on this site or in the product is personalised investment advice. Please read our
      <a href="/disclaimer" class="text-teal-300 underline hover:text-teal-200">full risk disclaimer</a>
      before making any trading decision.
    </p>
  </section>

  <CtaBanner
    title="Want to see the evidence for yourself?"
    description="Get early access and explore the technical, candlestick and AI/ML signals we've built — and the measured research behind them."
  />
</BaseLayout>
